{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"371db52820f91df86f071db88dc5f16a404cc96f7b859dbf2030fddf41fb7d7b","digest":{"component_or_area":"IAM access control for Bedrock API via instance role","key_entities":["rebar-gerrit-instance-role","infra/terraform/iam_s7.tf","bedrock:InvokeModel","bedrock:InvokeModelWithResponseStream","bedrock:Converse","arn:aws:bedrock:*::foundation-model/anthropic.claude-*","arn:aws:bedrock:*:896586841071:inference-profile/*.anthropic.claude-*","pydantic-ai BedrockProvider","IMDS","http_put_response_hop_limit","infra/runbooks/bedrock-access.md"],"problem_keywords":["bedrock access","iam grant","instance role","imds reachability","converse api","review-bot container"],"propositions":["The review-bot container requires IAM permissions to invoke Claude models via AWS Bedrock, currently absent from the instance role.","The correct IAM action for Bedrock Converse API calls is bedrock:InvokeModel (not bedrock:Converse), discoverable only through real instance-resident calls, not policy simulation.","IMDS is reachable from containers on the host; the instance role delivers credentials without raising http_put_response_hop_limit, so the solution is IAM-only with no network contingency needed.","The policy grant must be scoped to anthropic.claude-* foundation models and *.anthropic.claude-* inference profiles (with region wildcards for cross-region routing), not bedrock:* on *."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787731559886462001,"uuid":"11954e9e-f51d-4e69-90ba-841dfd65c5f8"}